1
00:00:01,625 --> 00:00:03,333
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:05,833
We can't let them get away
with that weapon!

3
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:08,625
H'yah!

4
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:14,333
[Nya] Slick move.

5
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:16,500
Now, stand back.

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,541
[sparking]

7
00:00:20,125 --> 00:00:22,916
Ugh! Are you wrecking my hair
on purpose?

8
00:00:22,916 --> 00:00:23,833
Ugh!

9
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:24,916
I got this!

10
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:27,541
Wait, wait, wait, Jay!
I'm standing in--

11
00:00:28,166 --> 00:00:29,916
N-n-n-no!

12
00:00:29,916 --> 00:00:31,250
[panting]

13
00:00:31,250 --> 00:00:32,833
What kind of Master of Lightning

14
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:35,208
forgets
water conducts electricity?

15
00:00:35,208 --> 00:00:38,041
Maybe the kind
who suffer from amnesia.

16
00:00:38,041 --> 00:00:39,750
Ugh, hate to say it, but...

17
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:40,916
that actually gave me
an idea.

18
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:43,666
Even though all of our powers
are on the fritz,

19
00:00:43,666 --> 00:00:45,333
maybe if we...

20
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:47,416
combine all three together?

21
00:00:48,458 --> 00:00:49,500
H'yah!

22
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:53,666
[powers surging]

23
00:00:59,208 --> 00:01:00,958
[♪♪♪]

24
00:01:06,833 --> 00:01:07,916
Ha!

25
00:01:07,916 --> 00:01:09,750
I'm a genius.

26
00:01:16,041 --> 00:01:17,708
[timer beeping]

27
00:01:17,708 --> 00:01:19,208
[blasting]

28
00:01:22,666 --> 00:01:23,625
What was that?

29
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:24,791
What'd they do?

30
00:01:24,791 --> 00:01:26,625
An electro-magnetic pulse.

31
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:28,750
Every vehicle here is fried.

32
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:30,916
[Nya] They really
don't want us following.

33
00:01:30,916 --> 00:01:32,916
[Kai] Well,
they got their wish.

34
00:01:32,916 --> 00:01:35,875
Crossing the Land of Madness
on foot takes forever.

35
00:01:35,875 --> 00:01:37,958
I speak from experience.

36
00:01:37,958 --> 00:01:39,000
The Samurai X Mech.

37
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,750
The D.B. Express.

38
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:42,041
The Earth Driller!

39
00:01:42,041 --> 00:01:44,708
Nya, you're like the greatest
engineer and inventor

40
00:01:44,708 --> 00:01:45,791
basically ever.

41
00:01:45,791 --> 00:01:47,750
Those memories are coming back?

42
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:49,166
I can't remember everything,

43
00:01:49,166 --> 00:01:50,750
but everything
I remember about you

44
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:52,000
is amazing.

45
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,958
But all you remember about me
is my bad ideas?

46
00:01:54,958 --> 00:01:56,416
What else is there?

47
00:01:56,416 --> 00:01:58,083
Fried circuits or not,

48
00:01:58,083 --> 00:01:59,750
I bet you can take
all these parts

49
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:02,583
and make us one working...
something?

50
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:06,625
Let's give it a shot!

51
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,833
[in Umbrasylvan accent]
Umbrasylvis is on lockdown

52
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:11,708
until the devious perpetrator

53
00:02:11,708 --> 00:02:14,375
who released the monster
on this humble burg

54
00:02:14,375 --> 00:02:16,916
can be identified, judged,

55
00:02:16,916 --> 00:02:18,125
and, most importantly,

56
00:02:18,125 --> 00:02:20,083
punished by a life sentence

57
00:02:20,083 --> 00:02:22,208
in the restraints
of excruciation!

58
00:02:22,208 --> 00:02:23,208
[townsfolk jeering]

59
00:02:23,208 --> 00:02:24,708
Uh...

60
00:02:24,708 --> 00:02:26,541
why is everyone shaking sticks?

61
00:02:26,541 --> 00:02:27,833
"Shaking"?

62
00:02:27,833 --> 00:02:30,916
They wag
Ancient Wagging Sticks,

63
00:02:30,916 --> 00:02:33,375
the traditional way
of expressing oneself

64
00:02:33,375 --> 00:02:35,291
in Umbrasylvan court.

65
00:02:35,291 --> 00:02:36,291
Everyone knows that!

66
00:02:36,291 --> 00:02:38,916
Now, there's a criminal
among us,

67
00:02:38,916 --> 00:02:41,666
and their evil must be purged!

68
00:02:41,666 --> 00:02:42,958
[blowing fanfare]

69
00:02:42,958 --> 00:02:44,750
[shouting angrily]

70
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:46,541
As Grand Inquisitor,

71
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:48,625
I hereby declare

72
00:02:48,625 --> 00:02:51,125
the inquisition begins!

73
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:53,208
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

74
00:02:53,208 --> 00:02:54,416
♪ So much to see ♪

75
00:02:54,416 --> 00:02:57,458
♪ Jump up, kick back
whip around and spin ♪

76
00:02:57,458 --> 00:02:59,166
♪ Together we will rise ♪

77
00:02:59,166 --> 00:03:00,416
♪ Whip around and spin ♪

78
00:03:00,416 --> 00:03:01,916
♪ Together we will rise ♪

79
00:03:01,916 --> 00:03:04,791
♪ For what's right ♪♪

80
00:03:06,208 --> 00:03:07,791
True or false.

81
00:03:07,791 --> 00:03:09,916
You are an outsider
to Umbrasylvis,

82
00:03:09,916 --> 00:03:11,791
and thus of suspicious
character and motive.

83
00:03:11,791 --> 00:03:13,250
Uh, false.

84
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:15,125
So you <i>aren't</i> an outsider?

85
00:03:15,125 --> 00:03:16,666
No... I mean, yes.

86
00:03:16,666 --> 00:03:18,375
We're not from here, but--

87
00:03:18,375 --> 00:03:19,958
Were you lying then
or lying now?

88
00:03:19,958 --> 00:03:20,958
Neither!

89
00:03:20,958 --> 00:03:22,583
[jeering]

90
00:03:22,583 --> 00:03:24,041
Don't you think a fountain

91
00:03:24,041 --> 00:03:26,416
is a suspicious way
to enter a city?

92
00:03:26,416 --> 00:03:27,500
Unless you're water.

93
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:28,833
Are you water?

94
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:30,041
What? No!

95
00:03:30,041 --> 00:03:32,166
We didn't come through
your fountain by choice.

96
00:03:32,166 --> 00:03:34,666
So you were sent here
under orders!

97
00:03:34,666 --> 00:03:36,125
That's not what I said!

98
00:03:36,125 --> 00:03:39,500
It seems there's a lot
you're not saying.

99
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:40,750
[townsfolk jeering]

100
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:41,875
Would you say you're known

101
00:03:41,875 --> 00:03:44,333
for how much
you like to fight, Wyldfyre?

102
00:03:44,333 --> 00:03:45,166
Of course!

103
00:03:45,166 --> 00:03:46,375
You wanna go right now?

104
00:03:46,375 --> 00:03:48,291
And would your associates
describe you

105
00:03:48,291 --> 00:03:51,083
as "thriving on chaos"?

106
00:03:51,083 --> 00:03:52,541
Duh.

107
00:03:52,541 --> 00:03:54,250
The kind of chaos
that might result from,

108
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:55,750
oh, I don't know,

109
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:58,125
releasing
a dangerous monster?

110
00:03:58,125 --> 00:04:01,208
Can I wear your tall hat?

111
00:04:01,208 --> 00:04:02,083
"Hat"?

112
00:04:02,083 --> 00:04:03,291
Hat?!

113
00:04:03,291 --> 00:04:04,708
Let the record show

114
00:04:04,708 --> 00:04:08,250
that the witness disrespected
the Mantle of Righteousness!

115
00:04:08,250 --> 00:04:09,916
[shouting angrily]

116
00:04:09,916 --> 00:04:13,041
I think it's obvious here
who the culprit is.

117
00:04:13,041 --> 00:04:14,875
She was with the dragon, sir.

118
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,958
The outsider known as Wyldfyre

119
00:04:17,958 --> 00:04:21,000
was in my windmill
with the dragon, Riyu,

120
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,166
all night.

121
00:04:22,166 --> 00:04:23,916
Wouldn't leave his side.

122
00:04:23,916 --> 00:04:26,875
She couldn't possibly
have let that monster out.

123
00:04:26,875 --> 00:04:28,291
Interesting,

124
00:04:28,291 --> 00:04:31,458
and were her companions
also with the dragon?

125
00:04:31,458 --> 00:04:33,166
Almost all night.

126
00:04:33,166 --> 00:04:34,458
"Almost"?

127
00:04:34,458 --> 00:04:36,166
But you can't account
for their whereabouts

128
00:04:36,166 --> 00:04:39,083
at every moment?

129
00:04:39,083 --> 00:04:41,375
Very interesting.

130
00:04:41,375 --> 00:04:44,875
The Explorers Club
adheres to strict regulations.

131
00:04:44,875 --> 00:04:46,083
Members are required

132
00:04:46,083 --> 00:04:48,083
to log their comings and goings
on the ship

133
00:04:48,083 --> 00:04:49,333
in this book.

134
00:04:49,333 --> 00:04:50,500
Now, as you can see,

135
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,875
each member of the expedition

136
00:04:51,875 --> 00:04:53,458
is accounted for last night.

137
00:04:53,458 --> 00:04:55,500
Those entries could've been
written whenever.

138
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,666
That's easily faked.

139
00:04:56,666 --> 00:04:57,666
Nonsense!

140
00:04:57,666 --> 00:04:59,333
These records are immaculate.

141
00:04:59,333 --> 00:05:01,333
No one with margins that clean

142
00:05:01,333 --> 00:05:03,000
would falsify records!

143
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,125
And do the names
of the other outsiders,

144
00:05:06,125 --> 00:05:08,333
these "nin-jah,"

145
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:10,666
appear anywhere in the logbook?

146
00:05:12,125 --> 00:05:12,958
No.

147
00:05:12,958 --> 00:05:14,166
Can you vouch

148
00:05:14,166 --> 00:05:16,666
for any of the "nin-jah" at all?

149
00:05:16,666 --> 00:05:18,458
No.

150
00:05:18,458 --> 00:05:19,458
I cannot.

151
00:05:21,958 --> 00:05:24,458
Isn't it true
that you were on the airship

152
00:05:24,458 --> 00:05:26,041
the night in question?

153
00:05:26,041 --> 00:05:27,250
I already told you,

154
00:05:27,250 --> 00:05:29,125
we went there
to get a cure for Riyu.

155
00:05:29,125 --> 00:05:30,916
And yet your names
do not appear

156
00:05:30,916 --> 00:05:33,583
on the aforementioned logbook.

157
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:36,375
We didn't even know
about that stupid book.

158
00:05:36,375 --> 00:05:37,708
[townsfolk gasping]

159
00:05:37,708 --> 00:05:39,375
So you snuck onto a ship,

160
00:05:39,375 --> 00:05:40,750
violated its regulations,

161
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:43,375
and released the monster
on an innocent population!

162
00:05:43,375 --> 00:05:45,125
That's not what happened!

163
00:05:45,125 --> 00:05:47,250
We shall see.

164
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:49,458
The Court must gather
additional facts

165
00:05:49,458 --> 00:05:50,958
based on today's testimony.

166
00:05:50,958 --> 00:05:52,416
In the meantime,

167
00:05:52,416 --> 00:05:54,791
bring forth the shame boards!

168
00:05:57,583 --> 00:06:00,250
"Warning: Dangerous Suspect."

169
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:02,250
Are these really necessary?

170
00:06:02,250 --> 00:06:03,791
[Grand Inquisitor]
Very much so.

171
00:06:03,791 --> 00:06:06,500
A Thread of Truth
is woven through each cord.

172
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:09,916
I will know if the signs
are removed.

173
00:06:09,916 --> 00:06:13,125
Such an act would result
in an immediate guilty verdict!

174
00:06:13,125 --> 00:06:15,666
This inquisition is in recess!

175
00:06:19,333 --> 00:06:21,666
I think I'd make
a pretty good Inquisitor

176
00:06:21,666 --> 00:06:22,916
since I'm always right,

177
00:06:22,916 --> 00:06:24,708
and I look good in hats.

178
00:06:24,708 --> 00:06:27,291
I can't believe my dad
wouldn't vouch for us.

179
00:06:27,291 --> 00:06:28,500
You saw someone with a mask

180
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,958
on that airship last night.

181
00:06:29,958 --> 00:06:32,583
Someone who probably
didn't sign that book either.

182
00:06:32,583 --> 00:06:33,625
Yeah...

183
00:06:33,625 --> 00:06:34,958
We gotta find that weirdo,

184
00:06:34,958 --> 00:06:37,000
or we'll be declared guilty
for sure.

185
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,166
Well, the Inquisitor
isn't the only one

186
00:06:39,166 --> 00:06:41,166
who knows how to inquire.

187
00:06:41,166 --> 00:06:42,708
Any clues
have to be on the airship.

188
00:06:42,708 --> 00:06:44,416
Let's go.

189
00:06:56,625 --> 00:06:58,375
I don't know how to help them.

190
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:04,500
[wheezing]

191
00:07:11,875 --> 00:07:12,708
[gasping]

192
00:07:15,166 --> 00:07:16,500
It's a seedling!

193
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:17,458
-[Acona chittering]
-Huh?

194
00:07:17,458 --> 00:07:19,166
[chittering]

195
00:07:19,166 --> 00:07:21,208
I think they want us
to plant it.

196
00:07:27,291 --> 00:07:31,041
<i>[Arc Dragon] I've never</i>
<i>seen the wood reach this point.</i>

197
00:07:31,041 --> 00:07:34,416
<i>I don't know</i>
<i>how much longer it--</i>

198
00:07:34,416 --> 00:07:35,875
<i>or I--</i>

199
00:07:35,875 --> 00:07:37,625
<i>can hold on,</i>

200
00:07:37,625 --> 00:07:39,958
<i>and if the Whispering Wood</i>
<i>falls,</i>

201
00:07:39,958 --> 00:07:42,875
<i>the Merged Lands</i>
<i>will eventually fall too.</i>

202
00:07:42,875 --> 00:07:45,625
[thudding heavily]

203
00:07:48,083 --> 00:07:51,541
<i>[Arc Dragon] You are...</i>
<i>comforting me?</i>

204
00:07:51,541 --> 00:07:55,000
<i>Though you are only</i>
<i>a simulation of life,</i>

205
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:59,000
<i>your emotions seem almost real.</i>

206
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,333
I may sometimes struggle
to communicate my feelings,

207
00:08:02,333 --> 00:08:05,833
but I feel them
as deeply as anyone else.

208
00:08:07,875 --> 00:08:08,833
[chittering]

209
00:08:13,541 --> 00:08:17,000
<i>[Arc Dragon] Thank you for</i>
<i>being with me at the very end.</i>

210
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,416
Maybe this isn't the end.

211
00:08:19,416 --> 00:08:21,083
Believe in Lloyd.

212
00:08:21,083 --> 00:08:22,500
There have been many times

213
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,250
when he's faced dire situations

214
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:26,000
and come out stronger.

215
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,125
<i>[Arc Dragon]</i>
<i>That is false hope.</i>

216
00:08:28,125 --> 00:08:29,416
<i>At his age,</i>

217
00:08:29,416 --> 00:08:31,750
<i>Lloyd is too deeply rooted</i>
<i>in his path</i>

218
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:34,291
<i>to cut himself free and live.</i>

219
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:42,083
[chittering excitedly]

220
00:08:42,083 --> 00:08:43,583
The Whispering Wood

221
00:08:43,583 --> 00:08:45,500
and its guardian,
the Green Ninja,

222
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:48,958
may be more resilient
than even you realize.

223
00:08:48,958 --> 00:08:50,500
[wind blowing]

224
00:08:54,958 --> 00:08:59,875
So, exactly how long
would I have kept that haircut?

225
00:08:59,875 --> 00:09:01,375
Whatever, dork.

226
00:09:01,375 --> 00:09:02,750
You wanna talk hair?

227
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:06,083
How old was I
when I forgot what a comb was?

228
00:09:06,083 --> 00:09:08,333
No wonder I still don't
have a girlfriend.

229
00:09:08,333 --> 00:09:09,541
Hey!

230
00:09:09,541 --> 00:09:11,791
I'm busy taking care
of a whole monastery, and--

231
00:09:11,791 --> 00:09:12,958
Whatever.

232
00:09:12,958 --> 00:09:14,750
Look, I'm here to prepare you

233
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:16,458
for the rest of the ritual.

234
00:09:16,458 --> 00:09:17,625
You?

235
00:09:19,250 --> 00:09:20,083
[grunting]

236
00:09:22,041 --> 00:09:23,750
You ready, punk?

237
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:32,333
Sometimes I think "exploring"
is just code for stealing.

238
00:09:32,333 --> 00:09:34,041
You really think
we're going to find a clue

239
00:09:34,041 --> 00:09:35,000
in one of these crates?

240
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,583
It'd help identify our suspect

241
00:09:36,583 --> 00:09:37,916
if we had a motive.

242
00:09:37,916 --> 00:09:40,333
They've gotta be
hiding something somewhere.

243
00:09:44,958 --> 00:09:45,875
Careful!

244
00:09:47,416 --> 00:09:48,833
Show-off.

245
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:49,708
Wha...!

246
00:09:49,708 --> 00:09:51,333
Oh!

247
00:09:54,625 --> 00:09:55,583
A-ha!

248
00:09:55,583 --> 00:09:57,083
A scale!

249
00:09:57,083 --> 00:09:58,541
We have our villain!

250
00:09:58,541 --> 00:09:59,666
Who?

251
00:09:59,666 --> 00:10:01,083
There's only one Explorer

252
00:10:01,083 --> 00:10:02,250
who could have left this!

253
00:10:02,250 --> 00:10:03,375
My father!

254
00:10:03,375 --> 00:10:05,333
You think your dad did it?

255
00:10:05,333 --> 00:10:06,541
You defended him

256
00:10:06,541 --> 00:10:08,958
when I suggested he maybe
wasn't such a great dad.

257
00:10:08,958 --> 00:10:11,833
Our relationship is...
complicated,

258
00:10:11,833 --> 00:10:13,541
but you heard him
at the inquisition.

259
00:10:13,541 --> 00:10:16,083
He couldn't put his neck
on the line for his own son.

260
00:10:16,083 --> 00:10:17,625
Why? He's guilty.

261
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:20,625
But the Expedition
has been using this ship

262
00:10:20,625 --> 00:10:21,625
for a while.

263
00:10:21,625 --> 00:10:23,041
Your dad could've
shed this scale

264
00:10:23,041 --> 00:10:25,041
at any point
during their travels.

265
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:26,083
Yeah.

266
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:27,291
The Inquisitor
is gonna need more

267
00:10:27,291 --> 00:10:28,458
to prove his guilt.

268
00:10:28,458 --> 00:10:30,208
Let's keep searching.

269
00:10:31,291 --> 00:10:32,791
After we heard that scream,
I came here,

270
00:10:32,791 --> 00:10:34,791
and found my dad wearing a mask,

271
00:10:34,791 --> 00:10:35,791
back there in the dark.

272
00:10:35,791 --> 00:10:37,583
We don't know it was your dad.

273
00:10:37,583 --> 00:10:39,416
I do. Come on.

274
00:10:39,416 --> 00:10:40,625
[grunting] Oh--

275
00:10:40,625 --> 00:10:41,625
[chuckling awkwardly]

276
00:10:43,041 --> 00:10:44,375
Ooh, sorry.

277
00:10:44,375 --> 00:10:45,750
[laughing]

278
00:10:45,750 --> 00:10:46,708
[grunting]

279
00:10:46,708 --> 00:10:47,708
Yeah.

280
00:10:50,250 --> 00:10:53,416
No door. No air vent.
No way out.

281
00:10:53,416 --> 00:10:54,833
Why would he free a monster

282
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:56,375
only to back himself
into a corner?

283
00:10:57,833 --> 00:10:58,833
Huh...

284
00:10:58,833 --> 00:10:59,833
this material looks newer

285
00:10:59,833 --> 00:11:01,416
than the rest of the corridor.

286
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:03,625
[clicking]

287
00:11:03,625 --> 00:11:04,458
[gasping]

288
00:11:04,458 --> 00:11:06,208
[hatch creaking open]

289
00:11:09,916 --> 00:11:10,958
Whoa!

290
00:11:10,958 --> 00:11:12,416
Blast from the past.

291
00:11:12,416 --> 00:11:13,750
It's Imperium tech,

292
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:17,125
the model that was used
in the Advanced Systems Lab.

293
00:11:17,125 --> 00:11:19,166
Where would my dad get that?

294
00:11:19,166 --> 00:11:20,791
Maybe it's stolen?

295
00:11:20,791 --> 00:11:22,416
[scoffing]
He's good at that.

296
00:11:22,416 --> 00:11:23,583
"Exploring."

297
00:11:23,583 --> 00:11:26,166
It's analyzing
the monster's energy signature

298
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:29,083
and searching for resonance
somewhere in Umbrasylvis.

299
00:11:29,083 --> 00:11:30,833
But you don't have to
break a monster loose

300
00:11:30,833 --> 00:11:32,041
to study it.

301
00:11:32,041 --> 00:11:34,208
Maybe they needed readings
as it moved around,

302
00:11:34,208 --> 00:11:36,541
to triangulate
synchronous energy sources.

303
00:11:36,541 --> 00:11:39,500
Oh, yes, the synchronous...
S-synchronous.

304
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:41,458
It's still processing
the readings,

305
00:11:41,458 --> 00:11:44,000
trying to find the location
of the resonant item,

306
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,500
but I might be able
to give it a boost if I--

307
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:49,250
There! Found the location.

308
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:51,666
We don't know
what he was searching for,

309
00:11:51,666 --> 00:11:53,208
but we do know where it is.

310
00:11:54,041 --> 00:11:55,416
You're putting it back?

311
00:11:55,416 --> 00:11:57,250
The only way
to prove their identity

312
00:11:57,250 --> 00:11:59,541
is to give them
exactly what they want...

313
00:11:59,541 --> 00:12:02,083
And be there to ambush them
when they try to get it.

314
00:12:02,083 --> 00:12:03,125
Ha!

315
00:12:03,125 --> 00:12:04,666
My dad won't see us coming!

316
00:12:05,666 --> 00:12:06,958
-[grunting]
-Whoa!

317
00:12:10,125 --> 00:12:11,791
Too slow!

318
00:12:11,791 --> 00:12:12,791
[laughing obnoxiously]

319
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:17,583
I forgot what a brat
I could be sometimes.

320
00:12:25,583 --> 00:12:27,375
You coming or not?

321
00:12:33,250 --> 00:12:35,166
Whoa! [grunting]

322
00:12:35,166 --> 00:12:36,500
[Tween Lloyd] What did I say?

323
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,583
I'm a path you didn't take,

324
00:12:38,583 --> 00:12:40,875
so take a different path.

325
00:12:41,916 --> 00:12:43,208
H'yah!

326
00:12:52,041 --> 00:12:54,625
What did you think
of your vision?

327
00:12:54,625 --> 00:12:56,958
I saw a network of roots.

328
00:12:56,958 --> 00:13:00,125
The trees were all...
connected somehow?

329
00:13:00,125 --> 00:13:02,041
And when one needed help,

330
00:13:02,041 --> 00:13:04,375
the others gave it nutrients.

331
00:13:04,375 --> 00:13:05,750
-[nearby] And...
-[gasping]

332
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:07,416
what does that tell you

333
00:13:07,416 --> 00:13:09,708
about the power
of the Green Ninja?

334
00:13:11,583 --> 00:13:14,166
Or do you need to get stuck
under the dirt again?

335
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,041
Aah!

336
00:13:19,166 --> 00:13:20,583
[screaming]

337
00:13:23,041 --> 00:13:24,250
Think.

338
00:13:24,250 --> 00:13:26,458
How did we get our powers?

339
00:13:26,458 --> 00:13:28,375
The Golden Weapons...

340
00:13:28,375 --> 00:13:31,041
and the other Ninja.

341
00:13:31,041 --> 00:13:33,041
They surrounded me.

342
00:13:33,041 --> 00:13:35,291
I could feel their energy,

343
00:13:35,291 --> 00:13:36,958
but what does that
have to do with--?

344
00:13:36,958 --> 00:13:38,625
Aah!

345
00:13:40,541 --> 00:13:42,875
[screaming]

346
00:13:42,875 --> 00:13:44,958
[grunting]

347
00:13:49,291 --> 00:13:51,250
Power comes from within,

348
00:13:51,250 --> 00:13:54,166
but... not all of it.

349
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:57,291
Some of our power comes from...

350
00:13:57,291 --> 00:13:59,916
those around us?

351
00:13:59,916 --> 00:14:01,125
Our friends,

352
00:14:01,125 --> 00:14:02,750
our family,

353
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:04,208
our community?

354
00:14:04,208 --> 00:14:05,125
[Tween Lloyd] Bingo.

355
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,666
Each tree is connected.

356
00:14:09,666 --> 00:14:11,583
Trees are life.

357
00:14:11,583 --> 00:14:13,958
You are the Master of Life.

358
00:14:13,958 --> 00:14:15,791
The Elemental Master of Life

359
00:14:15,791 --> 00:14:21,208
is the master of the connection
between and through all things.

360
00:14:24,333 --> 00:14:26,791
Just as you gained your powers

361
00:14:26,791 --> 00:14:28,541
through others'
connection to you,

362
00:14:28,541 --> 00:14:31,916
your true potential
can only manifest

363
00:14:31,916 --> 00:14:35,083
when you connect
to those around you.

364
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:38,416
[♪♪♪]

365
00:14:48,541 --> 00:14:51,833
It's beautiful, in a sad way.

366
00:14:51,833 --> 00:14:53,625
The Tree of Burdens.

367
00:14:53,625 --> 00:14:55,291
I overheard a local
talking about it.

368
00:14:55,291 --> 00:14:58,583
Each ribbon represents a worry.

369
00:14:58,583 --> 00:14:59,625
You tie a ribbon to the tree

370
00:14:59,625 --> 00:15:01,041
hoping its branches

371
00:15:01,041 --> 00:15:02,541
will help bear the weight
of your problem.

372
00:15:02,541 --> 00:15:05,166
Guess that's why
it's so twisted and bent.

373
00:15:05,166 --> 00:15:07,833
Wish I had a ribbon for my dad.

374
00:15:07,833 --> 00:15:09,000
Being perfect

375
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,208
was the only way
I could get his attention,

376
00:15:11,208 --> 00:15:13,541
but it was never enough.

377
00:15:13,541 --> 00:15:15,750
<i>I </i>was never enough.

378
00:15:18,375 --> 00:15:20,458
You're more than enough.

379
00:15:20,458 --> 00:15:22,500
Sometimes too much.

380
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:24,208
[footsteps approaching]

381
00:15:24,208 --> 00:15:25,708
[door opening]

382
00:15:25,708 --> 00:15:26,666
[Frak] That could be Dad.

383
00:15:26,666 --> 00:15:28,083
Quick, hide!

384
00:15:38,958 --> 00:15:42,041
[whispering]
Come on, let's grab him.

385
00:15:42,041 --> 00:15:44,000
Let's see what he wants
with the tree first.

386
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,583
It may be a clue to fighting
the Elemental Monsters.

387
00:15:48,791 --> 00:15:50,500
[beeping]

388
00:16:01,291 --> 00:16:03,541
What could that thing be?

389
00:16:03,541 --> 00:16:04,500
That's enough.

390
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:05,458
[Sora] Frak, wait!

391
00:16:05,458 --> 00:16:06,375
Stop!

392
00:16:06,375 --> 00:16:07,583
I know it's you, Dad!

393
00:16:11,958 --> 00:16:13,750
[weapon charging]

394
00:16:13,750 --> 00:16:15,458
[grunting]

395
00:16:16,791 --> 00:16:18,916
Leave my son alone!

396
00:16:20,041 --> 00:16:21,875
[gasping] Dad?

397
00:16:21,875 --> 00:16:22,916
How?

398
00:16:24,708 --> 00:16:25,958
Ha!

399
00:16:25,958 --> 00:16:27,625
Johnny Courageous?

400
00:16:27,625 --> 00:16:30,958
You betrayed
the Explorer's Club?

401
00:16:30,958 --> 00:16:33,750
Jolly bad form, old boy!

402
00:16:35,416 --> 00:16:38,333
[gasping] You <i>are </i>Imperian!

403
00:16:38,333 --> 00:16:40,375
Civil servant class?

404
00:16:40,375 --> 00:16:41,958
What did you take
from the Tree?

405
00:16:41,958 --> 00:16:44,791
Tell her
I don't speak to traitors.

406
00:16:44,791 --> 00:16:46,166
Traitor?

407
00:16:46,166 --> 00:16:48,166
I helped liberate Imperium!

408
00:16:48,166 --> 00:16:50,083
You helped it fall!

409
00:16:50,083 --> 00:16:53,125
All Hail The Good Empress!

410
00:16:53,125 --> 00:16:55,791
"The Good Empress"? What?

411
00:16:55,791 --> 00:16:56,750
[Frak] At least this Empress

412
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:58,000
won't get whatever this is--

413
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,541
[power surging]

414
00:16:59,541 --> 00:17:01,791
[rumbling]

415
00:17:01,791 --> 00:17:02,750
[gasping]

416
00:17:06,583 --> 00:17:07,625
[weapon charging]

417
00:17:09,458 --> 00:17:10,708
Something's happening!

418
00:17:10,708 --> 00:17:12,125
I can't control this!

419
00:17:12,125 --> 00:17:14,166
[Reggie]
It's going to be okay, son.

420
00:17:14,166 --> 00:17:15,750
[Frak gasps]

421
00:17:15,750 --> 00:17:17,166
[rumbling]

422
00:17:17,166 --> 00:17:18,666
You have to let it go.

423
00:17:18,666 --> 00:17:19,625
[straining]

424
00:17:21,041 --> 00:17:22,458
[rumbling stops]

425
00:17:23,458 --> 00:17:25,333
Yes, this handkerchief
was enchanted

426
00:17:25,333 --> 00:17:27,500
by the Pontifex Magicus
of Mysterium.

427
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,833
Not my first time
handling a cursed relic.

428
00:17:29,833 --> 00:17:32,250
We're, uh, gonna need that.

429
00:17:32,250 --> 00:17:33,208
Hopefully it will help
clear our name

430
00:17:33,208 --> 00:17:34,250
with the Inquisitor.

431
00:17:35,708 --> 00:17:36,875
Oh, right, right.

432
00:17:38,916 --> 00:17:40,250
Uh, sorry.

433
00:17:40,250 --> 00:17:41,291
I'm not all that familiar

434
00:17:41,291 --> 00:17:43,333
with handing over
rare artifacts.

435
00:17:47,208 --> 00:17:49,083
Thanks, Dad.

436
00:17:49,083 --> 00:17:50,833
I overheard you.

437
00:17:50,833 --> 00:17:52,125
You thought the villain...

438
00:17:52,125 --> 00:17:53,166
was me?

439
00:17:53,166 --> 00:17:54,500
I did.

440
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:56,333
'Cause it was easy to believe.

441
00:17:56,333 --> 00:17:57,500
Egads!

442
00:17:57,500 --> 00:17:58,833
I take offense.

443
00:17:58,833 --> 00:18:01,458
You didn't even try
to defend me in that court.

444
00:18:01,458 --> 00:18:02,875
But why would you have?

445
00:18:02,875 --> 00:18:04,833
You were never there for me
when I needed you.

446
00:18:04,833 --> 00:18:07,125
Gone for every
important moment in my life,

447
00:18:07,125 --> 00:18:10,750
chasing some discovery
that would be your legacy?

448
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:13,000
Guess you never thought
I could be your legacy.

449
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:14,083
[sighing]

450
00:18:14,083 --> 00:18:15,541
Frak, I just wanted you

451
00:18:15,541 --> 00:18:18,125
to have a father
you could be proud of.

452
00:18:18,125 --> 00:18:20,000
You don't know
what it used to be like

453
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,166
for Serpentine in Ninjago.

454
00:18:22,166 --> 00:18:25,291
"Never trust a snake,"
they used to say.

455
00:18:25,291 --> 00:18:28,250
I had to work twice as hard
for twice as long

456
00:18:28,250 --> 00:18:29,750
to get any recognition.

457
00:18:29,750 --> 00:18:31,041
Yeah, well,

458
00:18:31,041 --> 00:18:32,458
you didn't even work
half as hard

459
00:18:32,458 --> 00:18:33,583
at being a good dad.

460
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,666
Why'd the Temple
show you to me?

461
00:18:43,666 --> 00:18:46,416
I'd just accepted the incident
with Tomorrow's Tea

462
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:47,875
as another part of my destiny.

463
00:18:47,875 --> 00:18:50,000
The Ritual of Unrooting

464
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:53,416
requires you to understand
your connections to others,

465
00:18:53,416 --> 00:18:56,125
even to other yous.

466
00:18:56,125 --> 00:18:57,875
Who you were.

467
00:18:57,875 --> 00:18:59,666
Who you could have been.

468
00:18:59,666 --> 00:19:01,666
Who you might become.

469
00:19:03,291 --> 00:19:04,791
Remember that
for this next part.

470
00:19:04,791 --> 00:19:06,750
Uh, next part?

471
00:19:06,750 --> 00:19:09,000
This wasn't the test?

472
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:10,458
[chuckling]

473
00:19:10,458 --> 00:19:11,833
Are you serious?

474
00:19:11,833 --> 00:19:14,583
All this was just to give you
a fighting chance in there.

475
00:19:15,458 --> 00:19:17,458
[ground cracking]

476
00:19:23,041 --> 00:19:25,041
Meditate on your past

477
00:19:25,041 --> 00:19:27,500
and prepare for the future.

478
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:31,041
Through that archway
is your greatest foe.

479
00:19:31,041 --> 00:19:32,083
Who?

480
00:19:32,083 --> 00:19:34,791
An enemy you've faced
many times.

481
00:19:34,791 --> 00:19:37,333
One you've temporarily bested,

482
00:19:37,333 --> 00:19:39,791
but never truly defeated.

483
00:19:39,791 --> 00:19:40,750
Huh...

484
00:19:40,750 --> 00:19:43,375
That doesn't really
narrow it down.

485
00:19:43,375 --> 00:19:45,083
[Tween Lloyd] Only by
defeating this enemy

486
00:19:45,083 --> 00:19:46,833
will you be able
to fully connect

487
00:19:46,833 --> 00:19:49,166
to the pathways
of the Whispering Wood

488
00:19:49,166 --> 00:19:50,958
and embrace your power

489
00:19:50,958 --> 00:19:53,375
as the Legendary Green Ninja.

490
00:19:53,375 --> 00:19:55,166
Hey, wait.

491
00:19:55,166 --> 00:19:57,791
I know you're just
a manifestation,

492
00:19:57,791 --> 00:19:59,250
but I need to know...

493
00:19:59,250 --> 00:20:02,166
are you happy?

494
00:20:02,166 --> 00:20:04,708
You tell me.

495
00:20:06,916 --> 00:20:08,125
[Lloyd sighs]

496
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:11,291
[townsfolk murmuring]

497
00:20:11,291 --> 00:20:13,333
The inquisition
is back in session!

498
00:20:15,041 --> 00:20:16,500
[clearing his throat]

499
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:19,875
Well, if the accused
can't even bother to show up,

500
00:20:19,875 --> 00:20:21,916
that seems like proof enough.

501
00:20:21,916 --> 00:20:24,125
I hereby pronounce them guil--

502
00:20:24,125 --> 00:20:25,708
[Sora] Not so fast!

503
00:20:27,458 --> 00:20:29,000
Here's your culprit.

504
00:20:31,291 --> 00:20:33,458
He pulled this
out of the Tree of Burdens.

505
00:20:34,458 --> 00:20:36,500
[gasping]

506
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:38,083
Only a true villain

507
00:20:38,083 --> 00:20:40,125
would defile the sacred tree.

508
00:20:40,125 --> 00:20:42,833
I declare this miscreant guilty!

509
00:20:42,833 --> 00:20:43,833
[banging staff]

510
00:20:43,833 --> 00:20:44,750
These two are cleared

511
00:20:44,750 --> 00:20:46,291
of all suspicion!

512
00:20:46,291 --> 00:20:47,750
Lockdown lifted!

513
00:20:47,750 --> 00:20:50,083
Inquisition complete!

514
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:52,958
[blowing fanfare]

515
00:20:52,958 --> 00:20:54,375
-[crowd cheering]
-Whoa.

516
00:20:54,375 --> 00:20:56,958
[cheering]

517
00:20:58,250 --> 00:21:01,208
[Grand Inquisitor]
The only thing left to do now

518
00:21:01,208 --> 00:21:04,500
is deliver this
to the Good Empress...

519
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:06,416
[cheers turn to confusion]

520
00:21:06,416 --> 00:21:07,375
What?!

521
00:21:08,375 --> 00:21:11,000
[Umbrasylvan accent gone]
Endless months of deep cover

522
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,958
in this miserable backwater

523
00:21:12,958 --> 00:21:14,666
is finally over!

524
00:21:14,666 --> 00:21:17,125
You ignorant yokels,

525
00:21:17,125 --> 00:21:20,166
I'm part of the future,
not the past!

526
00:21:21,291 --> 00:21:24,750
All Hail The Good Empress.

527
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:25,666
[device beeping]

528
00:21:27,250 --> 00:21:29,875
[coughing]

529
00:21:33,208 --> 00:21:34,916
[gasping] Where did he--?

530
00:21:34,916 --> 00:21:37,250
[engines whirring overhead]

531
00:21:37,250 --> 00:21:39,166
He's taking the airship!

532
00:21:39,166 --> 00:21:41,500
If Empress Beatrix
is really back,

533
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:44,125
we're all in more danger
than we ever imagined!

534
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,875
[♪♪♪]

